technology stack
- frontend: React Native with Expo
- database: SQLite
- state management: Redux or Context API
- offline support: SQLite for local storage and synchronization to other users with superbase when online
- backend: Supabase (for authentication, data synchronization, cloud functions)
- authentication: Google OAuth
- deployment: Expo Application Services (EAS) for building and deploying mobile apps
- testing: Jest and React Native Testing Library for unit and integration tests

non functional requirements
- performance: app should load within 3 seconds, smooth navigation
- security: data encryption, secure authentication
- scalability: design database and architecture to handle growing user base
- usability: intuitive UI/UX design, easy navigation
- maintainability: clean code, modular architecture, comprehensive documentation
- compatibility: support for both iOS and Android devices
- accessibility: comply with accessibility standards for users with disabilities
- localization: support for multiple languages and regional settings
- support and maintenance: regular updates, bug fixes, user support channels
- support for dark mode and light mode themes

